WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.867
Matthew, Chapter Eleven.

2
00:00:01.867 --> 00:00:10.133
And it came to pass, when Jesus had made an end of commanding his twelve disciples, he departed thence to teach and to preach in their cities.

3
00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:20.533
Now when John had heard in the prison the works of Christ, he sent two of his disciples, And said unto him, Art thou he that should come, or do we look for another?

4
00:00:20.533 --> 00:00:35.867
Jesus answered and said unto them, Go and shew John again those things which ye do hear and see: The blind receive their sight, and the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, and the deaf hear, the dead are raised up, and the poor have the gospel preached to them.

5
00:00:35.867 --> 00:00:39.600
And blessed is he, whosoever shall not be offended in me.

6
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:47.333
And as they departed, Jesus began to say unto the multitudes concerning John, What went ye out into the wilderness to see?

7
00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:49.333
A reed shaken with the wind?

8
00:00:49.333 --> 00:00:52.133
But what went ye out for to see?

9
00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:54.133
A man clothed in soft raiment?

10
00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:58.267
behold, they that wear soft clothing are in kings' houses.

11
00:00:58.267 --> 00:01:00.400
But what went ye out for to see?

12
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:00.800
A prophet?

13
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.533
yea, I say unto you, and more than a prophet.

14
00:01:04.533 --> 00:01:11.600
For this is he, of whom it is written, Behold, I send my messenger before thy face, which shall prepare thy way before thee.

15
00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:21.600
Verily I say unto you, Among them that are born of women there hath not risen a greater than John the Baptist: notwithstanding he that is least in the kingdom of heaven is greater than he.

16
00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:28.133
And from the days of John the Baptist until now the kingdom of heaven suffereth violence, and the violent take it by force.

17
00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:31.333
For all the prophets and the law prophesied until John.

18
00:01:31.333 --> 00:01:35.467
And if ye will receive it, this is Elias, which was for to come.

19
00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:38.267
He that hath ears to hear, let him hear.

20
00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:40.933
But whereunto shall I liken this generation?

21
00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:52.267
It is like unto children sitting in the markets, and calling unto their fellows, And saying, We have piped unto you, and ye have not danced; we have mourned unto you, and ye have not lamented.

22
00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:58.267
For John came neither eating nor drinking, and they say, He hath a devil.

23
00:01:58.267 --> 00:02:06.400
The Son of man came eating and drinking, and they say, Behold a man gluttonous, and a winebibber, a friend of publicans and sinners.

24
00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:09.067
But wisdom is justified of her children.

25
00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:18.000
Then began he to upbraid the cities wherein most of his mighty works were done, because they repented not: Woe unto thee, Chorazin!

26
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.600
woe unto thee, Bethsaida!

27
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:27.733
for if the mighty works, which were done in you, had been done in Tyre and Sidon, they would have repented long ago in sackcloth and ashes.

28
00:02:27.733 --> 00:02:34.533
But I say unto you, It shall be more tolerable for Tyre and Sidon at the day of judgment, than for you.

29
00:02:34.533 --> 00:02:46.133
And thou, Capernaum, which art exalted unto heaven, shalt be brought down to hell: for if the mighty works, which have been done in thee, had been done in Sodom, it would have remained until this day.

30
00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:52.933
But I say unto you, That it shall be more tolerable for the land of Sodom in the day of judgment, than for thee.

31
00:02:52.933 --> 00:03:03.067
At that time Jesus answered and said, I thank thee, O Father, Lord of heaven and earth, because thou hast hid these things from the wise and prudent, and hast revealed them unto babes.

32
00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:07.467
Even so, Father: for so it seemed good in thy sight.

33
00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:19.067
All things are delivered unto me of my Father: and no man knoweth the Son, but the Father; neither knoweth any man the Father, save the Son, and he to whomsoever the Son will reveal him.

34
00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:24.267
Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest.

35
00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:32.000
Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall find rest unto your souls.

36
00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.600
For my yoke is easy, and my burden is light.

